# Code guideline modules (index)

These **`.mdc`** files govern **architectural patterns** for native
Android apps. They live in the **`android-kotlin-rules`** repository and
are consumed via a **git submodule** at each app repo's
**`.cursor/rules/`** (this directory when mounted).

**Product-specific** requirements, ADRs, screen catalogs, and env URLs
belong in each app repo under **`docs/specification/`** and **README** —
not in this package.

## Sourcing principle

Every rule below names its **primary source** first. Where Google/AOSP has
an official position (an Android Developers architecture guide, the
Kotlin coding conventions, a Jetpack library's own docs, Material 3),
that is the primary source and is never contradicted by a third-party
convention. Third-party libraries (Retrofit, Timber, Sentry, PostHog,
MockK, Turbine, Roborazzi) are the **production-composition or
enforcement layer on top** — adopted because they solve a real problem
better than a hand-rolled equivalent, not because Google lacks an
opinion. Where Google genuinely has no first-party option (networking has
none), the module says so rather than inventing a source.

Android's ecosystem is more first-party than iOS's in several places:
**Hilt** (DI), **Room** (persistence), **WorkManager** (background work),
and **Navigation Compose** (routing) are all Jetpack's own official
recommendations.

## Process rules (this package)

| File | Topic |
|------|--------|
| **`spec-driven-development.mdc`** | SDD truth hierarchy, as-built discipline, PR traceability |
| **`testing-verify-flows.mdc`** | JUnit4 / Compose Testing / MockK / Turbine methodology, gate ladder |
| **`android-adr.mdc`** | ADR triggers, template, and the growth path for ADR-gated features |

## Architectural rules (this package)

| File | Topic |
|------|--------|
| **`project-structure-gradle.mdc`** | Gradle + version catalogs as the base; convention plugins as an optional modularization layer |
| **`architecture-udf-state.mdc`** | Google's UDF (state down, events up); `ViewModel` + `StateFlow<UiState>`; "MVI-flavored MVVM" convention |
| **`dependency-injection-hilt.mdc`** | Hilt as the default DI framework; Koin only via ADR |
| **`coroutines-flow.mdc`** | Kotlin Coroutines, structured concurrency, `Flow`/`StateFlow` |
| **`networking-api-client.mdc`** | Retrofit + OkHttp composition (Interceptor + Authenticator); typed errors |
| **`persistence-room.mdc`** | Room as the default local persistence |
| **`app-lifecycle-background.mdc`** | Activity/Process lifecycle, `ViewModel` scoping, WorkManager |
| **`navigation-deep-linking.mdc`** | Navigation Compose, App Links, App Actions/Shortcuts |
| **`push-notifications.mdc`** | Firebase Cloud Messaging registration and handling |
| **`compose-composition.mdc`** | Composable decomposition, state hoisting, no logic in composables |
| **`design-tokens-accessibility.mdc`** | Material 3 tokens, TalkBack, scalable text, accessibility checks |
| **`kotlin-style-conventions.mdc`** | Android Kotlin style guide; ktlint + detekt enforcement |
| **`logging-observability.mdc`** | Logcat + Timber, Sentry crash reporting |
| **`no-hardcoded-strings.mdc`** | String resources (`strings.xml`) + Compose `stringResource()` |
| **`security-baseline-mobile.mdc`** | DataStore + Keystore (Tink), BiometricPrompt, network security config |
| **`privacy-permissions.mdc`** | Runtime permissions, Play Console Data Safety |
| **`product-analytics.mdc`** | Event-tracking convention; PostHog default, Firebase Analytics ADR-gated alternative |

## Explicitly out of scope (see README + `android-adr.mdc`)

Release-pipeline mechanics, a handful of product-specific feature
categories, and other-platform companion apps are intentionally not
covered here — see the README's "Explicitly out of scope" table and
`android-adr.mdc`'s growth path for how a scoped addition gets adopted
when a product actually needs one.

## Per-repository product documentation

Each app repo should provide (not in this package):

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`docs/specification/product/`** | Requirements, capabilities, features |
| **`docs/specification/adr/`** | Architecture decision records |
| **`docs/specification/as-built/`** | What is live today |
| **`app/README.md`** or a **`Tests/README.md`**-equivalent | Verify/debug commands, feature map |
| **`README.md`** | Setup, run commands |

## Cross-project conventions

- **Do not** add product features or screen names to shared **`.mdc`** files — extend **`docs/specification/`** in the consumer repo.
- **Do not** edit **`.cursor/rules/`** in consumer repos — propose changes via PR on the upstream `android-kotlin-rules` repository.
- **Do not** add release/signing/CI-pipeline content to **`.mdc`** files — enforced by `scripts/check_mdc_boundary.sh`.
- **No emojis** in code, logs, or UI copy; use Logcat priority levels (`Log.d`/`Log.i`/`Log.w`/`Log.e`) via Timber instead of emoji status markers.

## Where to start

1. **`architecture-udf-state.mdc`** and **`dependency-injection-hilt.mdc`** for structure and composition.
2. **`spec-driven-development.mdc`** before changing any behavior.
3. Consumer repo **`docs/specification/`** when the task changes behavior, screens, or integrations.
